    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45-a3">

                <pb facs="0332" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg118"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 3.</seg></opener>
                <head>Frederick F. Low to H. C. Blake</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">On board Flag-ship
                            Colorado</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-05-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 23,
                    1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With this you will find a general letter
                    which I had prepared for your guidance during your preliminary trip to the
                    northward. Inasmuch as you will not proceed as far as the island of Kang-hoa
                    before returning to the flag-ship, I do not send the letter for transmission to
                    the King of Corea. I shall retain it here; and if you meet any officials
                    desirous of learning the object of our visit to the coast, you will be guided by
                    the tenor of the general letter accompanying this in your conversations with
                    them. You will further inform them that I am on board the flag-ship, and have a
                    letter which I desire to send to the government.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. F. LOW.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
